            "review_title": "Review at King Dongas",
            "review_text": "bennett2006\nHo Chi Minh City590 contributions\n1\nBest and biggest Korean pork cutlet in HCMC ... so far\nJul 2019 • Solo\nLook at the size of that pork cutlet!! This is the first time I'm seeing such a huge pork cutlet - Korean-style - in HCMC. It comes with rice, salad, fresh vegetables, kim chi and seaweed soup. For 120,000vnd, it's a steal. But I was suspicious. Given the price and size, it'll probably taste like crap. My first mouthful confirmed my second visit here soon. Damn, it's really good. And the accompanying sauce was delicious too ... and sufficient for the whole huge cutlet (which is not the case always). I almost couldn't finish the generous portion, but finally I did myself proud. Be sure to come here when you're famished. By the way, the price is nett and so my bill came to 140,000vnd (with a 20k Fanta). Great meal, great price ... I'm coming back soon. I put the price as mid-range with reference to a normal Vietnamese budget.\n\nBy the way, it's located just next to Pico Plaza (Lottemart) along Cong Hoa Street. For those not familiar, it's about 10-15 min from the airport. Not very convenient for tourists but for those who live and work around here, it's a refreshing difference from the normal restaurants around.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 18, 2019",
